@copilot Please fix the JDK 27 CI failure in this test. In https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/actions/runs/38951432856/job/117172397357, `byteBuffer3` fails on all six executions, including retries, because `verify(mockHandler).afterDefineClass(eq(null))` expects one invocation but receives three. The class-definition assertions and the target `beforeDefineClass(...)` verification pass.

The mock handler is global, and class-loading and lambda instrumentation share its exit callback. Unstubbed entry methods return null, so verifying `afterDefineClass(null)` also counts unrelated exits. Return a distinct mocked `DefineClassContext` from the entry callback for the target loader and class bytes, configure that stub before installing the global handler, and verify `afterDefineClass(same(context))` instead. Keep the exact-once entry verification and successful class-definition assertions. Do not hard-code three invocations or weaken the assertion to `atLeastOnce()`.

Run the targeted `DefineClassInstrumentationTest` on JDK 27 and the default JDK. Keep this fix scoped to the test unless further evidence demonstrates a production defect.

